[77.441, "o", "m"]
[77.507, "o", "\r\n"]
[79.307, "o", "\r\n"]
[79.857, "o", "\u001b[38;5;253m●\u001b[0m Flux's whole design is continuous reconciliation — it re-applies on an\r\n"]
[81.207, "o", "  interval, git change or not. It would have re-scaled your eleven\r\n"]
[82.357, "o", "  deliberately-stopped workloads on the next tick and called it\r\n"]
[83.507, "o", "  convergence. Argo with selfHeal off applies on merge, and only then.\r\n"]
[86.307, "o", "\r\n"]
[86.857, "o", "\u001b[38;5;253m●\u001b[0m So: cloudflare-iac + aws-iac → GitHub Actions with OIDC and the destroy\r\n"]
[88.207, "o", "  gate · k3s-iac → Argo CD, no selfHeal, no prune · nixos-iac → comin,\r\n"]
[89.357, "o", "  each host pulls and builds itself. Canary first, control plane last.\r\n"]
